{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 11521 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "1067074038741a7a350def0eb39c455b02c857eed9894508c6a9c6ffdb2f1d2f" :edb/db-before-t 11520 :edb/db-after-t 11521 :edb/tx-data [[13194139544833 50 #inst "2026-10-30T01:43:49.420Z" 13194139544833 17592186576411 true] [17592186054992 1071 "![](images/ae/aee38b4fa46a403ee9517fc5a087434c8205b6553a4ebefa43be74ba7babfbc0.png)\n\nUsing the graphical method, find the solutions $(x,y)$ of the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y=x+1 \\\\ y={x}^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" 13194139544833 17592186576411 true] [17592186054992 1071 "![](images/ae/aee38b4fa46a403ee9517fc5a087434c8205b6553a4ebefa43be74ba7babfbc0.png)\n\nUsing the graphical method, find the solutions $(x,y)$ of the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}y=x+1 \\\\ y={x}^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139544833 17592186576411 false] [17592186060191 1074 "We will graph each branch separately.\n\n- On the interval $(-\\infty ,1],$ we have a line with slope $2$ and $y$-intercept $1.$ So the graph is the line $y=2x+1$ that ends at $(1,3),$ including this point.\n\n- On the interval $(1,\\infty )$, we have a line with a slope of $-2$ that passes through the point $(1,0).$ We can find the equation of this line using point-slope form:\n\n$$\ny-0=-2(x-1)\\,⟹\\,y=2-2x\n$$\n\nSo the graph is the line $y=2-2x$ that starts at $(1,0),$ excluding this point.\n\nTherefore, the function is defined as follows:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+1,\\, & x\\le 1 \\\\ 2-2x,\\, & x>1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" 13194139544833 17592186576411 true] [17592186060191 1074 "We will graph each branch separately.\n\n- On the interval $(-\\infty ,1],$ we have a line with slope $2$ and $y$-intercept $1.$ So the graph is the line $y=2x+1$ that ends at $(1,3),$ including this point.\n\n- On the interval $(1,\\infty )$, we have a line with a slope of $-2$ that passes through the point $(1,0).$ We can find the equation of this line using point-slope form:\n\n$$\ny-0=-2(x-1)\\,⟹\\,y=2-2x\n$$\n\nSo the graph is the line $y=2-2x$ that starts at $(1,0),$ excluding this point.\n\nTherefore, the function is defined as follows:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+1,\\, & x\\le 1 \\\\ 2-2x,\\, & x>1\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139544833 17592186576411 false] [17592186063975 1071 "What is the solution to the following system of inequalities?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x-35\\ge 0 \\\\ 7x>21\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" 13194139544833 17592186576411 true] [17592186063975 1071 "What is the solution to the following system of inequalities?\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5x-35\\ge 0 \\\\ 7x>21\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139544833 17592186576411 false] [17592186063978 1071 "What is the solution to the following system of inequalities?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2-7x\\ge 2 \\\\ 10x-3\\ge 7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" 13194139544833 17592186576411 true] [17592186063978 1071 "What is the solution to the following system of inequalities?\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2-7x\\ge 2 \\\\ 10x-3\\ge 7\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139544833 17592186576411 false] [17592186064474 1071 "Let ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{20}$ be a random sample of size $n=20$ from a population with probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}, & -1\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nGiven that the population variance ${\\sigma }^{2}=0.6,$ calculate $P(0<\\overset{―}{X}<0.2).$\n\n*Hint: Assume that the sample size is sufficiently large for the central limit theorem to be applied. A table of values of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution.* \n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\"> <th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$z$</th><th dat