egin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-2L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}+3L\\{1\\}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+2={X}_{1}(s)-2{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-0=-{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{3}{s}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\},$ and we have used the fact that $L\\{1\\}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the second equation for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s) & =-{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{3}{s} \\\\ (s+1){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{3}{s} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{3}{s(s+1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the first equation and solving for ${X}_{1}(s)$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+2 & ={X}_{1}(s)-2{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-1){X}_{1}(s) & =-2-2{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-1){X}_{1}(s) & =-2-2\\left(\\frac{3}{s(s+1)}\\right) \\\\ (s-1){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{-2s(s+1)-6}{s(s+1)} \\\\ (s-1){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{-2({s}^{2}+s)-6}{s(s+1)} \\\\ (s-1){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{-2{s}^{2}-2s-6}{s(s+1)} \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{-2{s}^{2}-2s-6}{s(s+1)(s-1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{-2{s}^{2}-2s-6}{s(s-1)(s+1)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{3}{s(s+1)}.\n$$" 13194139544833 17592186576411 true] [17592186541069 1074 "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-{x}_{2}(t)+3\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-2L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}+3L\\{1\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+2={X}_{1}(s)-2{X}