 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" 13194139544833 17592186576411 false] [17592186552229 1080 "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-3x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-2y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right." 13194139544833 17592186576411 true] [17592186552229 1080 "\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-3x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-2y(t)\\end{aligned}" 13194139544833 17592186576411 false] [17592186552237 1080 "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}0.002{y}^{2}, & -10<y<0 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right." 13194139544833 17592186576411 true] [17592186552237 1080 "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0.002{y}^{2}, & -10<y<0 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" 13194139544833 17592186576411 false] [17592186552239 1080 "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}12{e}^{-12y},\\, & y>0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right." 13194139544833 17592186576411 true] [17592186552239 1080 "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}12{e}^{-12y},\\, & y>0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" 13194139544833 17592186576411 false] [17592186552243 1080 "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{10}\\sqrt{\\frac{y}{5}}, & 1\\le y<5 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\\right." 13194139544833 17592186576411 true] [17592186552243 1080 "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{10}\\sqrt{\\frac{y}{5}}, & 1\\le y<5 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}" 13194139544833 17592186576411 false] [17592186552244 1080 "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-0.02y, & -10<y<0 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right." 13194139544833 17592186576411 true] [17592186552244 1080 "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-0.02y, & -10<y<0 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" 13194139544833 17592186576411 false] [17592186552403 1071 "Let $X$ be a continuous random variable with the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x,\\, & -1<x<0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nIf $Y=10X,$ then what is the probability density function of $Y?$" 13194139544833 17592186576411 true] [17592186552403 1071 "Let $X$ be a continuous random variable with the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x,\\, & -1<x<0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $Y=10X,$ then what is the probability density function of $Y?$" 13194139544833 17592186576411 false] [17592186552403 1074 "To compute the probability density function of a random variable $Y,$ where $Y=u(X)$ is a continuous, strictly monotonic function of a continuous random variable $X,$ we follow two steps:\n\n- First, we find an expression for ${F}_{Y}$ terms of ${F}_{X},$ where ${F}_{Y}$ and ${F}_{X}$ are the cumulative distribution functions of $Y$ and $X,$ respectively.\n\n- Then, we differentiate ${F}_{Y}$ to get the probability density function ${f}_{Y}.$\n\nBefore we start, note that $Y=10X$ is a strictly increasing function of $X.$ Moreover, for $-1<x<0,$ we have $-10<y<0.$\n\n![](images/4b/4b03f4d44db5b0db0498469f80fa25e56177a8602c657d8506105837212bf5ba.png)\n\n*Note: Image not drawn to scale.*\n\nNow, using the definition of the cumulative distribution of $Y,$ for $-10<y<0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{Y}(y) & =P(Y\\le y) \\\\  & =P(10X\\le y) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 0.1y) \\\\  & ={F}_{X}(0.1y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo compute the PDF ${f}_{Y}(y)$ for $-10<y<0,$ we differentiate ${F}_{Y}$ with respect to $y$ using the chain rule. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={F}_{Y}^{′}(y) \\\\  & =0.1\\cdot {F}_{X}^{′}(0.1y) \\\\  & =0.1\\cdot {f}_{X}(0.1y).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the definition of ${f}_{X},$ we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & =0.1\\cdot {f}_{X}(0.1y) \\\\  & =0.1\\cdot (-2)\\cdot 0.1y \\\\  & =-0.02y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for the PDF of $Y$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-0.02y, & -10<y<0 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" 13194139544833 17592186576411 true] [17592186552403 1074 "T