re the cumulative distribution functions of $Y$ and $X,$ respectively.\n\n- Then, we differentiate ${F}_{Y}$ to get the probability density function ${f}_{Y}.$\n\nBefore we start, note that $Y=\\sqrt[3]{X}$ is a strictly increasing function of $X.$ Moreover, for $1<x<8,$ we have $1<y<2.$\n\n![](images/21/21d19426e86916c123e898bf5427ef858784a601eedb861ba55e22855912005c.png)\n\n*Note: Image not drawn to scale.*\n\nNow, using the definition of the cumulative distribution of $Y,$ for $1<y<2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{Y}(y) & =P(Y\\le y) \\\\  & =P(\\sqrt[3]{X}\\le y) \\\\  & =P(X\\le {y}^{3}) \\\\  & =F({y}^{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo compute the PDF ${f}_{Y}(y)$ for $1<y<2,$ we differentiate ${F}_{Y}$ with respect to $y$ using the chain rule. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={F}_{Y}^{′}(y) \\\\  & =3{y}^{2}\\cdot {F}_{X}^{′}({y}^{3}) \\\\  & =3{y}^{2}\\cdot {f}_{X}({y}^{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the definition of ${f}_{X},$ we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & =3{y}^{2}\\cdot {f}_{X}({y}^{3}) \\\\  & =3{y}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{({y}^{3})^{2}}} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for the PDF of $Y$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\, & 1<y<2 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" 13194139544833 17592186576411 true] [17592186659668 1074 "To compute the probability density function of a random variable $Y,$ where $Y=u(X)$ is a continuous, strictly monotonic function of a continuous random variable $X,$ we follow two steps:\n\n- First, we find an expression for ${F}_{Y}$ terms of ${F}_{X},$ where ${F}_{Y}$ and ${F}_{X}$ are the cumulative distribution functions of $Y$ and $X,$ respectively.\n\n- Then, we differentiate ${F}_{Y}$ to get the probability density function ${f}_{Y}.$\n\nBefore we start, note that $Y=\\sqrt[3]{X}$ is a strictly increasing function of $X.$ Moreover, for $1<x<8,$ we have $1<y<2.$\n\n![](images/21/21d19426e86916c123e898bf5